SDLC (Software Development Life Cycle) and STLC (Software Testing Life Cycle) 
______________________________________________________________________________________________________________

SDLC (Software Development Life Cycle)

Definition: A structured process followed to design, develop, test, and deploy software.
Phases:
Requirement Analysis – Gather and document user needs.
Planning – Define scope, resources, timelines, and risks.
Design – Create system architecture and detailed design.
Development – Actual coding of the software.
Testing – Verify functionality, performance, and quality.
Deployment – Release software to production.
Maintenance – Bug fixes, updates, and enhancements.
Goal: Deliver high-quality software that meets customer requirements.

STLC (Software Testing Life Cycle)

Definition: A sequence of activities performed during testing to ensure software quality.
Phases:
Requirement Analysis – Understand what needs to be tested.
Test Planning – Define strategy, scope, resources, and schedule.
Test Case Development – Write test cases and prepare test data.
Test Environment Setup – Configure hardware/software for testing.
Test Execution – Run test cases and log defects.
Defect Reporting & Tracking – Communicate issues to developers.
Test Closure – Evaluate test results, prepare reports, and lessons learned.
Goal: Ensure the software is bug-free and meets quality standards.

************************************************************************************************
Phases of SDLC
Requirement Analysis
Gather requirements from stakeholders.
Document functional and non-functional needs.
Output: Software Requirement Specification (SRS).

Planning
Define scope, resources, cost, and timeline.
Risk analysis and feasibility study.
Output: Project plan.

Design
High-level design (architecture).
Low-level design (modules, database schema).
Output: Design Document.

Development (Coding)
Actual implementation of the design.
Developers write code in chosen programming language.
Output: Source code.

Testing
Verify software against requirements.
Includes unit, integration, system, and acceptance testing.
Output: Tested software.

Deployment
Release software to production environment.
May include beta release, pilot testing.
Output: Working product.

Maintenance
Bug fixes, updates, enhancements.
Continuous support and monitoring.
Output: Stable, improved system.

Software Testing Life Cycle (STLC)
Definition:  
STLC is a sequence of activities performed by the QA/testing team to ensure software quality. 
It runs parallel to SDLC but focuses only on testing aspects.

Phases of STLC
Requirement Analysis
Understand testable requirements from SRS.
Identify test objectives and scope.
Output: Requirement Traceability Matrix (RTM).

Test Planning
Define testing strategy, tools, resources, and schedule.

Risk analysis for testing.
Output: Test Plan document.
Test Case Development
Write detailed test cases and test scripts.

Prepare test data.
Output: Test cases/test data.
Test Environment Setup
Configure hardware/software for testing.

Ensure test environment is ready.
Output: Test environment.
Test Execution
Run test cases.

Log defects in defect tracking tool.
Output: Test execution report.
Defect Reporting & Tracking
Report bugs to developers.

Track defect status until closure.
Output: Defect logs.
Test Closure

Evaluate test completion criteria.
Prepare test summary report.
Output: Test closure report.






